From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: apklayer <apklayer@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] SandboxClassLoader: array and slash names, app classes

apklayer patch (docs/PATCHES.md): ART's class loaders answer array class names ("[Ljava.lang.String;",
which Chromium's JNI layer asks for) and binary names with slashes (Paddleboat loads "com/google/.../GameControllerManager");
Robolectric's loadClass did neither. A name the sandbox cannot find is asked of the app's own class loader through
ApklayerAppHook (runtime/patches, apklayer's own), because framework and Robolectric code load app classes by name through the
sandbox. Formerly a bytecode rewrite (runtime/patches/apklayer/patches/SandboxLoaderPatch.java).

Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION). Applied by scripts/build-runtime-overlay.sh onto the staged
upstream sources (<native>/aosp/robolectric-src); the result is compiled into native-runtime.jar ahead of Robolectric_all.jar.
---
diff --git a/sandbox/src/main/java/org/robolectric/internal/bytecode/SandboxClassLoader.java b/sandbox/src/main/java/org/robolectric/internal/bytecode/SandboxClassLoader.java
--- a/sandbox/src/main/java/org/robolectric/internal/bytecode/SandboxClassLoader.java
+++ b/sandbox/src/main/java/org/robolectric/internal/bytecode/SandboxClassLoader.java
@@ -151,8 +151,26 @@
     return null;
   }
 
+  // apklayer patch: ART's class loaders answer array names ("[Ljava.lang.String;", Chromium's JNI asks) and binary names with
+  // slashes (Paddleboat); a name the sandbox lacks is the app's, whose classes have a loader of their own (ApklayerAppHook)
   @Override
   public Class<?> loadClass(String name, boolean resolve) throws ClassNotFoundException {
+    name = name.replace('/', '.');
+    if (name.startsWith("[")) {
+      return Class.forName(name, false, this);
+    }
+    try {
+      return sandboxLoadClass(name, resolve);
+    } catch (ClassNotFoundException missing) {
+      Class<?> own = ApklayerAppHook.appClass(name);
+      if (own == null) {
+        throw missing;
+      }
+      return own;
+    }
+  }
+
+  private Class<?> sandboxLoadClass(String name, boolean resolve) throws ClassNotFoundException {
     synchronized (getClassLoadingLock(name)) {
       Class<?> loadedClass = findLoadedClass(name);
       if (loadedClass != null) {
